#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:19
msgid "What is Everest Base Camp (EBC)?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:20
msgid ""
"Everest Base Camp is the starting point for climbers attempting to summit "
"Mount Everest, the highest peak in the world. It is located at an altitude "
"of approximately 5,364 meters (17,598 feet) above sea level in the Khumbu "
"region of Nepal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:24
msgid "How do I get to Everest Base Camp?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:25
msgid ""
"The most common way to reach Everest Base Camp is by trekking from Lukla, a "
"small mountain airstrip in Nepal. You can take a flight from Kathmandu to "
"Lukla and start your trek from there. The trek usually takes around 12-14 "
"days round trip."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:31
msgid "Trekking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:35
msgid "Do I need previous trekking experience to reach EBC?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:36
msgid ""
"While previous trekking experience can be helpful, it is not mandatory. The "
"Everest Base Camp trek is challenging but can be undertaken by anyone with "
"a good level of fitness and a strong determination to complete the journey."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:40
msgid "When is the best time to trek to Everest Base Camp?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trip-widgets/faqs/demo.php:41
msgid ""
"The best time for the Everest Base Camp trek is during the pre-monsoon "
"(spring) season (March to May) and post-monsoon (autumn) season (September "
"to November). During these months, the weather is relatively stable, and "
"the skies are clear, providing breathtaking views of the Himalayas."
msgstr ""

